{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1382973-instruments-in-m20-again","id":1382973,"title":"Instruments in M20 (again)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-21T08:24:05-07:00","id":1382973,"title":"Instruments in M20 (again)","content":"I know this has been discussed before in the past. I am not skilled at threadomancy, and I have (maybe) a different take on the subject.<br /> <br /> I have been going back and forth with different ideas on how to mix elements of Awakening into M20. I keep scrapping and revising in an effort to keep it simple and elegant. The concepts I am interested in are Wisdom, Mudras (Rote Skills), and Yantras (Tools and etc). But what first got me interested in *that* was trying to wrap my head around M20 Instruments. The manner in which they are transcended, and what requires what, is purposefully vague. I believe that the idea was to give players and gms greater creative liscence, and I do appreciate that.<br /> So, without the boring details of all the permutations of ideas I had, going forward this is what I have in mind for a campaign I am planning.<br /> <br /> As for Wisdom, I want to make it the threshold for backlash rolls. Instead of a static 5, a mage makes a backlash roll if the Paradox gain equals or exceeds their Wisdom score. Said score rises and falls as normal in Awakening (and the MTG).<br /> <br /> As for Mudras, I was at first thinking of just grafting this on. But I changed my mind and am taking a cue from the Enlightened Grimoire. There, the optional rule is that when you learn a Rote, you get to attach it to a Sphere, and add that score to your Arete roll. My twist is that each Rote learned is attached to an Ability as per the Paradigm of the mage who invented that Rote and/or wrote it down.<br /> <br /> Now, getting to my point with Instruments. My idea is that, as Arete rises, instead of transcending the need for individual instruments, go back to the idea of transcending the need to use Instruments on a Sphere by Sphere basis. But there is no link between Sphere and specific Instrument. You can use any instrument, it is just a matter of whether or not you need one. Then, on top of that, allow mages to combine multiple Instruments to add to their casting roll.<br /> <br /> As an add on, My thoughts for Willpower in magic. Willpower caps the casting bonus from a Rote Ability and multiple Instruments. Further, Willpower is the limit of how many rounds of Extended casting one may perform.<br /> <br /> Thoughts and feedback?<br /> I just want to add the *right* amount of spice. Keep the hr's simple but flavorful. Looking at what I just wrote, maybe even this is tooo much and I need to dial back a tad.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T10:09:55-07:00","id":1382994,"title":"","content":"I'll have more thoughts later, once I've had a chance to digest this. But for now: if you're not going to discard instruments by choosing which instruments to discard, you might want to consider discarding instruments based on how powerful the magick is rather than which Spheres are used in it. For example: at Arete 2, you can perform one-dot Effects without instruments; at Arete 4, you can also perform two-dot Effects without instruments; and so on, with every +2 Arete adding one to the rank of Effects that you can perform without instruments. For technomancers, the thresholds come at Arete 6, 7, 8, 9, and 10 instead of 2, 4, 6, 8, and 10. Basically, I treat this as a variation of the Automatic Successes option, where sufficient Arete lets you pull off small Effects without even needing to roll. <br /> <br /> Alternately, just do away with the business of high Arete letting you dispense with Instruments entirely. The first Yantra you use with a casting is \u201cmandatory\u201d and provides a reduced benefit if it provides any benefit at all; if you want to perform the Effect without instruments, use the \u201cSurpassing your Focus\u201d option. A variation on this would be to say that the amount of \u201cmandatory Yantras\u201d is based on the number of Successes that needed to be achieved to accomplish the Effect: small Effects don't require much in the way of preparation, but big Effects do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}